BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T220000
LOCATION:Burbank Auditorium - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:SRJC Bands: Pandora's Box
DESCRIPTION:SRJC Symphonic Band &amp\; Jazz Band explore humanity's impac
 t on the planet in a concert featuring video projections\, Erik Johnson &
 amp\; Jazz Mirage.  SRJC Symphonic Band and Jazz Band present a powerful 
 multimedia concert exploring humanity\, community\, and our impact on the
  world around us.  Through music and video projections by Nancy Hayashiba
 ra\, the program examines questions of identity\, environmental responsib
 ility\, division\, and connection. Who are we as a country? Is there room
  for everyone? Can we come together as a community in the face of violenc
 e\, racism\, and conflict?  This one-of-a-kind performance invites audien
 ces to reflect on the challenges of our time through music\, imagery\, an
 d artistic collaboration.  7pm - Preshow with Jazz Mirage.Buy tickets her
 e! (https://www.eventbrite.com/e/srjc-bands-pandoras-box-wvideo-projectio
 ns-erik-johnson-jazz-mirage-tickets-1986100939374)&#160\;View the music d
 epartment's events list here. (https://music.santarosa.edu/events)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  SRJC Symphonic Band &amp\; Jazz Band ex
 plore humanity's impact on the planet in a concert featuring video projec
 tions\, Erik Johnson &amp\; Jazz Mirage.</p><p>  SRJC Symphonic Band and 
 Jazz Band present a powerful multimedia concert exploring humanity\, comm
 unity\, and our impact on the world around us.</p><p>  Through music and 
 video projections by Nancy Hayashibara\, the program examines questions o
 f identity\, environmental responsibility\, division\, and connection. Wh
 o are we as a country? Is there room for everyone? Can we come together a
 s a community in the face of violence\, racism\, and conflict?</p><p>  Th
 is one-of-a-kind performance invites audiences to reflect on the challeng
 es of our time through music\, imagery\, and artistic collaboration.</p><
 p>  7pm - Preshow with Jazz Mirage.</p><p><a href="https://www.eventbrite
 .com/e/srjc-bands-pandoras-box-wvideo-projections-erik-johnson-jazz-mirag
 e-tickets-1986100939374" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buy tickets here!
 </a>&#160\;</p><p><a href="https://music.santarosa.edu/events" target="_b
 lank" rel="noopener">View the music department's events list here.</a></p
 >
